[Applause]  welcome to the show well  this morning i was thinking about our  guest today gwyneth paltrow and i am so  excited to talk to her about  co-parenting  and i've learned one of the most  important life lessons from my tiny  existence which is i cannot  control things because so much of the  time you know i just don't get that  luxury of things being exactly the way i  would like them to be  and i have learned that it is my  reaction  i can control and we're going to talk  about it when you have to co-parent and  figuring that out not only is it an art  but it is within our control of how we  deal with it with our kids  and all i ever want to do is make my  kids feel  safe and again we can't control  everything  but we can have a true part in how i  conduct myself within  our family and i can't wait to talk  about it because it's such a big part of  my world and my kids really are  my priority another thing i couldn't  control  this weekend was i took frankie to the  aquarium  and we drove an hour and we watched the  river out our car windows and  i hugged the curves and my minivan  through the lanes like i was coloring in  a book it was sunday  and when we finally got there  unfortunately i didn't know you had to  make reservations  and we were not able to get in because  rules are rules  and that's the lesson i tried to teach  frankie i certainly didn't want to teach  her the wrong thing in that moment  but then of course i asked the lady if i  gave her some cash could she look the  other way  and she said ma'am you can make  reservations online  book your tickets with an unmovable tone  and i said  oh god please no i'm not a payer offer  normally i just thought since you were  closing soon anyway and i just think  your bosses should actually know what an  amazing person you are  that you will simply not break the rules  but then i was curious has anyone ever  else ever tried to find a clever way in  when like the signs say no  entry so to speak i love receiving a no  after i've tried everything and if you  have a story without breaking the law of  course  if you do have one i want to hear it  okay  have you tried to figure out how to get  your kid into a sold-out aquarium type  of thing  go to twitter and send us your story and  use the hashtag  worldbendingparent so good news frankie  learned that things don't always go as  planned and things aren't always within  our control  and we went to nathan's hot dogs and i  found one open carnival game and  we played all the money that woman  wouldn't take and good for her  and we drove home happy and life was  good and when you know your kids are  truly happy  not because they got what they wanted  but because plan b was just as good  well that was my morning share and now  let's get  into some important and awesome things  taking place in and around  our world it's time for drew's news  [Applause]  sir ma'am guy ma'am  i asked you a question  [Music]  tell me your story  it's drew's news  do you ever feel overwhelmed by the  tidal wave of news out there  well relax we've got you covered we sift  through it all to find a few nuggets to  start your day and here we go let's see  what  made the papers excuse me  frog and throat hang on  ah the detroit news is reporting  something that sparked my interest  lego is going to swap out its plastic  packaging  in favor of paper packaging  and all because kids demanded it  however lego pieces are still incredibly  painful to step on and maybe they can  work on that next  these kids make me feel so optimistic  i mean lego is a huge brand this will  have a giant impact  reducing plastic is so important my  friend cameron diaz i'm not name  dropping she just happens to be my  friend  she used to get on me for the last 20  years she was so ahead of the curve you  know she's always been  environmentally conscious and she used  to turn off all my lights and my pool  heater and  tell me to go get a hybrid car and you  know i finally i've switched i've made  our promise a year ago and  i drink out of these paper water  companies which i  they show that the packaging is possible  and they taste delicious i really love  them  and i have this metal cup that's missing  i'll show you later and  i used to drink out of styrofoam so like  this is a big deal for me and  i'm one small person i don't think i can  make a big change  and when i see something like lego is  doing this then i think change is  possible  and if we all continue to be mindful  about these things we can change our  world for our kids  but again parents when you're screaming  after stepping on one of those legos  that's okay too so moving on  our next story because that's what  happens when you step on a lego  this story warmed my heart in a radio  interview the other day usher shared  this story behind his latest single i  cry and he's quoted as saying  that he didn't have a relationship with  his father and so when he was watching a  movie with his two young sons and there  was an emotional  father-son moment on screen he started  to cry  and then his sons were shocked and they  asked him are you crying dad and  he said that he took that moment to say  yeah i am  crying and that it was okay and a song  was born  thank you usher we should be teaching  boys that it's okay to cry at an early  age  and he says that empathy can bring us  all closer together incredibly  difficult times such as we're in and i  couldn't agree more  so it turns out men are crying now more  than ever  welcome to the club  [Music]  you

